    "title": "bug(scm,win32): worker-auth T5 fails Step 5 — host gh.exe wins over fake gh.cmd (/user exit 1)",
    "status": "completed",
    "narratives": {
      "Description": "bug(scm,win32): worker-auth T5 fails Step 5 — host gh.exe wins over fake gh.cmd (/user exit 1)",
      "Origin": "Ingested from https://github.com/deftai/directive/issues/5081",
      "Overview": "## Summary\nWindows `task release` Step 5 fails `worker-auth-cli.integration.test.ts` T5 (assigned host-gh admitted on ambiguous runtime). Exit 2 with `SCM not ready: gh auth status passed but GitHub /user failed: exit 1`. Tip Linux TypeScript CI is green on the same SHA.\n\n## Evidence\n- Release cut `0.119.10` Step 5: `Tests 3 failed | 19172 passed` (2026-09-28).\n- Isolated: `pnpm exec vitest run packages/core/src/scm/worker-auth-cli.integration.test.ts` — T5 fails; T1/T2/T4/subdir pass.\n- Repro stderr: `gh auth status passed but GitHub /user failed: exit 1`.\n- Fake-gh `calls.log` empty in a harness repro → product `which(\\\"gh\\\")` likely resolving the real host `gh.exe` instead of the PATH-prepended fake `gh.cmd`.\n- Sibling false failures from `DEFT_SKIP_TS_BUILD=1` leaking into `ts-build-fresh.test.ts` (fixed by not exporting that env for Step 5; also harden the test to clear skip in fail cases).\n\n## Acceptance\n- [ ] T5 passes on win32 with the existing fake-gh PATH prepend (no host `gh.exe` steal).\n- [ ] `ts-build-fresh` fail cases pass even when parent env has `DEFT_SKIP_TS_BUILD=1`.\n- [ ] CHANGELOG [Unreleased] Fixed bullet.\n- [ ] Windows `task release` Step 5 can proceed past this class (no T5 / ts-build-fresh env false fail).\n\n## Refs\nBlocks release `0.119.10`. Child of #5016 / #3663 worker-auth surface.\r\n\n",
      "Labels": "bug"
    },
